screensaver-settings(1)

# NAME

screensaver-settings - choose a screen saver

# SYNOPSIS

*screensaver-settings*

# DESCRIPTION

A window for choosing a screen saver, in the classic arrangement: a picture of a
monitor showing the one chosen, a list to choose from, *Settings* and *Preview*
buttons, how long to wait, and whether to lock the screen on return.

Choosing *(None)* turns the screen saver off. Choosing *(Random)* shows a
different one each time; its *Settings* button chooses which.

Applying the settings enables and starts *screensaverd*(1) for the user.

# SEE ALSO

*screensaverd*(1), *screensaverctl*(1)
